From: hashtagbasit <53941105+hashtagbasit@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: mangmi-pocket-max: trigger travel from the fixed rest reading

Same as the Retroid pad: the trigger samples were taken from the
calibrated trigger_*_max, which calibration rewrites, so after one a full
press fell short of the range. Measure from the MCU's rest reading
(MCU_BRAKE_MAX / MCU_GAS_MAX) and stop clamping to the calibrated maximum,
so the next calibration can measure the whole travel.

--- a/drivers/input/joystick/mangmi-pocket-max.c	2026-10-10 02:07:01
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/mangmi-pocket-max.c	2026-10-10 02:07:18
@@ -211,13 +211,19 @@
 	return DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(v * MCU_AXIS_OUT, MCU_MAP_ZONE);
 }
 
-static int mcu_trigger(u16 raw, int trigger_max, int deadzone, int antideadzone)
+/*
+ * rest is the raw reading with the trigger released (the MCU counts down as
+ * it is pressed), not the calibrated trigger_*_max: that one is only the
+ * reported range. Not clamped to it either, so a later calibration can see
+ * the full travel.
+ */
+static int mcu_trigger(u16 raw, int rest, int deadzone, int antideadzone)
 {
-	int v = trigger_max - (int)raw;
+	int v = rest - (int)raw;
 
 	if (v < deadzone)
 		return 0;
-	return clamp(v - antideadzone, 0, trigger_max - antideadzone);
+	return max(v - antideadzone, 0);
 }
 
 struct mcu_gpio_btn {
@@ -458,12 +464,12 @@
 
 	if (var->ch_tl >= 0)
 		input_report_abs(dev, ABS_HAT2X,
-				 mcu_trigger(adc[var->ch_tl], trigger_left_max,
+				 mcu_trigger(adc[var->ch_tl], MCU_BRAKE_MAX,
 					     trigger_left_deadzone,
 					     trigger_left_antideadzone));
 	if (var->ch_tr >= 0)
 		input_report_abs(dev, ABS_HAT2Y,
-				 mcu_trigger(adc[var->ch_tr], trigger_right_max,
+				 mcu_trigger(adc[var->ch_tr], MCU_GAS_MAX,
 					     trigger_right_deadzone,
 					     trigger_right_antideadzone));
 
